binfmt_misc: flag E, the binary is the process's executable

Under binfmt_misc /proc/<pid>/exe is the interpreter, so every program run
through qemu-arm is "qemu-arm" to whatever identifies a peer by its
executable; webOS's ls-hubd does, and refuses every client. With the new
flag E (which implies O) begin_new_exec() records the binary itself as
mm->exe_file, as after a native exec. Entries registered without it behave
as before; its status file lists the flag.

--- a/Documentation/admin-guide/binfmt-misc.rst
+++ b/Documentation/admin-guide/binfmt-misc.rst
@@ -88,6 +88,12 @@
 	    emulation is installed and uses the opened image to spawn the
 	    emulator, meaning it is always available once installed,
 	    regardless of how the environment changes.
+      ``E`` - executable
+            The process's executable (``/proc/<pid>/exe``, ``mm->exe_file``)
+            is usually the interpreter. When this flag is included, it is the
+            binary, as after a native exec, so programs that identify a peer
+            by its executable see the program rather than its interpreter. It
+            implies the ``O`` flag.
 
 
 There are some restrictions:
